何？「撮りますよ～」
What? "Taking the picture now~"

186
00:13:56,356 --> 00:13:59,756
え、ここ空いてるからここ入れってことじゃない？
Wait, it's open right here, so doesn't that mean I should go here?

187
00:13:59,856 --> 00:14:01,756
笑顔で！はーい！
With a smile! Okaaay!

188
00:14:01,956 --> 00:14:05,356
わし偉い人なのかな？真ん中が不自然に開けられていた。
Am I an important person? The center was unnaturally left open.

189
00:14:05,756 --> 00:14:08,256
わしにここに来いということ。
Meaning they want me to come here.

190
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:12,556
上手！え、今回かなり正解率高いかも！
Well done! Whoa, my accuracy might be super high this time!

191
00:14:13,156 --> 00:14:16,756
1、2回で学べている予感！あ、あ、足ね。はい。
I feel like I've learned from the first couple times! Ah, the legs, right. Okay.

192
00:14:17,256 --> 00:14:20,156
通るときにね、足伸ばしたら邪魔だよね。
If you stretch your legs out when someone passes, you're in the way, right?

193
00:14:20,356 --> 00:14:24,156
映画館とかでもね、あの、人が通るとき用にね、足をどけたりね。
Even in movie theaters, you tuck your legs in when people walk past.

194
00:14:24,656 --> 00:14:28,056
え、今まですっごい空気読めてる予感！
Whoa, I feel like I've been reading the room better than ever!

195
00:14:28,556 --> 00:14:31,256
持久走大会きたー！
Endurance running contest is here!

196
00:14:31,456 --> 00:14:33,456
持久走といえば「一緒に走ろうね」
When it comes to long-distance running, it's always "Let's run together, okay?"

197
00:14:33,556 --> 00:14:35,956
あー！「二人で一緒にゴールしようね！」来た！
Aah! "Let's cross the finish line together!" Here it is!

198
00:14:37,256 --> 00:14:41,356
え、わしさ、これ、これ系でさ、待ってもらえたことないんだけど。
Wait, I've never had anyone actually wait for me in this kind of situation, though.

199
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:45,256
わし、これ系で待ってもらったことないんだけど。
I've never once had someone wait for me in this sort of thing.

200
00:14:45,456 --> 00:14:48,256
だからわしは待つよ、友人。
So I will wait for you, friend.

201
00:14:48,356 --> 00:14:51,356
気持ち分かるよ、おぬしの。わし持久走で一番ドベじゃったからね。
I understand your feelings. I was always dead last in long-distance running, after all.

202
00:14:51,456 --> 00:14:52,556
だいたい。
Basically always.

203
00:14:52,856 --> 00:14:55,556
よいしょ。よいしょー！
Heave-ho. Yaaay!

204
00:14:56,556 --> 00:14:58,056
え、来た。
Oh, here it comes.

205
00:14:58,356 --> 00:15:01,156
え、今回かなり100点なんじゃないの？
Wait, aren't we basically at 100 points this time?

206
00:15:01,356 --> 00:15:04,056
あからさ...「あからさま」だって！あからさま！
Blatan... "Blatantly," it says! Blatantly!

207
00:15:04,156 --> 00:15:07,056
ね、あからさまに読めてるってことはさ、
Hey, if it's blatantly reading the room, does that mean...

208
00:15:06,151 --> 00:15:06,831
あ
Ah,

209
00:15:07,031 --> 00:15:08,831
あからさまってさー
When they say "blatantly"...

210
00:15:09,481 --> 00:15:11,981
かなり最上級じゃない？お主ら。
isn't that the highest tier, everyone?

211
00:15:12,831 --> 00:15:15,681
空気を読みマスターがいるとしたら
If there is a room-reading master out there,

212
00:15:16,031 --> 00:15:17,881
わしのことなんじゃない？
wouldn't that be me?

213
00:15:21,181 --> 00:15:23,681
ちなみに持久走ガチで苦手だった。
By the way, I was seriously awful at long-distance running.

214
00:15:24,031 --> 00:15:26,131
あの持久力に本当に自信がない。
Like, I truly have zero confidence in my endurance.

215
00:15:26,831 --> 00:15:28,531
あの何事においてもね。
In absolutely everything, really.

216
00:15:28,881 --> 00:15:32,531
走るとかもじゃし、全ての持久力に自信がなかったのじゃ。
Running, sure, but I had zero endurance across the board.

217
00:15:33,031 --> 00:15:36,031
[Title: 第11問]
[Title: Question 11]

218
00:15:35,031 --> 00:15:35,931
来た。
Here we go.

219
00:15:36,931 --> 00:15:38,431
始まった。紙の空気読み。
It started. Paper room-reading.

220
